{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519974-have-you-tried-to-create-your-own-disciplines","id":1519974,"title":"Have you tried to create your own disciplines?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-06T11:16:47-07:00","id":1519974,"title":"Have you tried to create your own disciplines?","content":"I never tried self as I don\u2019t have that level of creativity for trying to make something like that out of the cloth and stick to creating amalgam powers from existing disciplines.<br /> <br /> But that is just me and I\u2019m sure some of you tried to create your own home brewed powers and how did it go for you and your games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T19:56:12-07:00","id":1520007,"title":"","content":"Age ago, like back in 2nd edition, I tried to work out a discipline that let vampires fly like the ones in the Anne Rice books. I never really went anywhere with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T00:43:19-07:00","id":1520021,"title":"","content":"As I think I've mentioned before I don't like signature Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Hence I haven't had a flash of inspiration for a concept that could actually become a Discipline in itself that would work for me and what I want from and in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T09:06:20-07:00","id":1520040,"title":"","content":"Once. Back in the mid 90s, when i was in boarding school, had a little too much time without nothing to do and no internet in sight, i got in my head the idea of attempting to rearrange the core clans so that everyone also had a favored/signature discipline of their own.<br /> <br /> With Tremere having Thaumaturgy, Gangrel with Protean, pushing Dementation on Malkavians (kind of an easy-lazy idea even before VtDA was a thing) - and giving the Ventrue <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Sovereign\" target=\"_blank\">Sovereign</a> in place of Presence - that was more than half the job done before i even began, so i felt the task reasonably feasible and fair.<br /> <br /> I then started to work on the Brujah and making a discipline called Flamen, that played with anger, passion and frenzy, while having some concept of a discipline related to playing with perception and the senses for the Toreador.<br /> <br /> And then when halfway through the Brujah it hit me &quot;Wait, but if the Brujah &amp; Ventrue drop Presence, the Toreador* are left as its signature users by elimination! Do i <b>want</b> that?&quot;<br /> <br /> *Yes, i know <b><i>technically</i></b> there would still be the Setites &amp; Baali around with favored Presence still, but it did bring home the &quot;what is clan signature, what is too many or not&quot; issue, what along with the fact half the powers i had inserted in Flamen were simply Animalism &amp; Presence i had pilfered and reframed, made me realize that replacing already existing disciplines with newer ones could quickly devolve into a slippery slope of an ever more confused mess.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sometime after that i started thinking of Garou gifts, how they are much more freeform within the frame of Auspice, Breed &amp; Tribe and decided to go into the opposite direction, eliminating signature disciplines altogether and setting up &quot;alternate clan branches&quot; within some of the core disciplines, what honestly has worked pretty nicely overall in the games i've STed through the years.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-07-2023, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}